WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.000
EPA 608 is not optional. You cannot legally touch refrigerant without it.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:30.000
DOT — the Department of Transportation — regulates refrigerant cylinders. Every
cylinder has a DOT specification stamped on the collar: the spec number, working
pressure, water capacity, tare weight, and hydrostatic test date.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Cylinders must be hydrostatically retested every 5 years. An expired test date
means the cylinder cannot legally be refilled.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Recovery cylinders are gray with yellow tops — that is the DOT standard color.
Never fill any cylinder above 80 percent of its water capacity. Disposable
cylinders cannot be refilled. It is illegal and dangerous.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:15.000
Record keeping: technicians must keep records of refrigerant purchases and
disposals for 3 years and make them available for EPA inspection.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Check the hydrostatic test date before every recovery job. An expired cylinder
at a supply house is a red flag. Do not use it.

